  1/5 (fifth)              0.20273255            1.500000
  1/7 (fourth)             0.14384104            1.333333
  3/5 (ln2 rapidity)       0.69314718            4.000000
  ln(2)                    0.85398805            5.517783
  pi/4                     1.05930617            8.319585

  arctanh(1/phi) = 0.7218177376
  = (3/2)*ln(phi) = 0.7218177376
  Match: True
  Because Q(1/phi) = phi^3, so rapidity = ln(phi^3)/2 = (3/2)*ln(phi).

  arctanh(1/tau) = 0.6093778634
  = ln(tau) = 0.6093778634
  Match: True
  Because Q(1/tau) = tau^2, so rapidity = ln(tau^2)/2 = ln(tau).

  THE RAPIDITY OF 1/phi IS (3/2)*ln(phi).
  THE RAPIDITY OF 1/tau IS ln(tau).
  The golden ratio gets a factor of 3/2 (the PERFECT FIFTH!).
  The tribonacci gets a factor of 1 (the UNISON).

  In musical terms:
  phi-rapidity = ln(phi) transposed up a fifth
  tau-rapidity = ln(tau) at the fundamental

============================================================
4. RAPIDITY ARITHMETIC: THE ADDITIVE STRUCTURE
============================================================

  Rapidity adds. This means we can do ARITHMETIC in rapidity space.

  rapidity(2) = ln(2)/2 = 0.346574
  rapidity(3) = ln(3)/2 = 0.549306
  rapidity(6) = ln(6)/2 = 0.895880 = rapidity(2) + rapidity(3)
  Verify: 0.346574 + 0.549306 = 0.895880 = 0.895880

  MULTIPLICATION in Z maps to ADDITION in rapidity space.
  This is the FUNDAMENTAL THEOREM OF ARITHMETIC restated:
  rapidity(n) = sum of rapidity(p) over prime factors p of n.

  n    rapidity(n)    = sum of prime rapidities
  -------------------------------------------------------
       6     0.895880   = ln(2)/2 + ln(3)/2
      10     1.151293   = ln(2)/2 + ln(5)/2
      12     1.242453   = ln(2)/2 + ln(2)/2 + ln(3)/2
      15     1.354025   = ln(3)/2 + ln(5)/2
      21     1.522261   = ln(3)/2 + ln(7)/2
      30     1.700599   = ln(2)/2 + ln(3)/2 + ln(5)/2
      42     1.868835   = ln(2)/2 + ln(3)/2 + ln(7)/2
     105     2.326980   = ln(3)/2 + ln(5)/2 + ln(7)/2
     189     2.620874   = ln(3)/2 + ln(3)/2 + ln(3)/2 + ln(7)/2
   95095     5.731316   = ln(5)/2 + ln(7)/2 + ln(11)/2 + ln(13)/2 + ln(19)/2

  RAPIDITY OF 21 = ln(3)/2 + ln(7)/2 = ln(21)/2
  = 1.522261
  = rapidity(curvature quantum) + rapidity(hyperbolic threshold)

  RAPIDITY OF 189 = ln(3^3*7)/2 = 3*ln(3)/2 + ln(7)/2
  = 2.620874
  = 3*(rapidity of curvature) + rapidity of threshold
  = THREE OCTAVES above the threshold!

  RAPIDITY OF 95095 = ln(5*7*11*13*19)/2
  = 5.731316
  = sum of rapidities of five Paley-adjacent primes

