  gap * 2p approaches 2 as p -> inf (by PNT: p_{n+1}/p_n -> 1).
  ln(p_{n+1}/p_n) ~ (p_{n+1}-p_n)/p_n ~ 2/p_n (average gap ~ ln(p)).

  TWIN PRIMES in rapidity space:
  Twin primes (p, p+2) have rapidity gap = ln(1+2/p)/2 ~ 1/p.
    (3,5): rapidity gap = 0.25541281 ~ 1/3 = 0.33333333
    (5,7): rapidity gap = 0.16823612 ~ 1/5 = 0.20000000
    (11,13): rapidity gap = 0.08352704 ~ 1/11 = 0.09090909
    (29,31): rapidity gap = 0.03334569 ~ 1/29 = 0.03448276
    (41,43): rapidity gap = 0.02381402 ~ 1/41 = 0.02439024
    (101,103): rapidity gap = 0.00980424 ~ 1/101 = 0.00990099

  Twin primes are points that are VANISHINGLY CLOSE in rapidity space.
  The twin prime conjecture: there are infinitely many rapidity-near pairs.

============================================================
6. RAPIDITY AND INFORMATION THEORY
============================================================

  The Fisher-Rao metric on Bernoulli distributions is ds^2 = dp^2/(p(1-p)).
  The geodesic distance between p and q is |2*arctanh(2p-1) - 2*arctanh(2q-1)|.
  Reparametrize: theta = 2*arctanh(2p-1), so p = (1+tanh(theta/2))/2.
  Then ds^2 = d(theta)^2. The rapidity IS the natural parameter!

  A coin with bias p has Fisher-Rao position theta = 2*arctanh(2p-1).
  The fair coin p=1/2 has theta = 0 (origin).

  Coin bias vs rapidity position:
    p = 0.01: theta =  -4.5951
    p = 0.10: theta =  -2.1972
    p = 0.20: theta =  -1.3863
    p = 0.30: theta =  -0.8473
    p = 0.40: theta =  -0.4055
    p = 0.50: theta =  +0.0000
    p = 0.60: theta =  +0.4055
    p = 0.70: theta =  +0.8473
    p = 0.80: theta =  +1.3863
    p = 0.90: theta =  +2.1972
    p = 0.99: theta =  +4.5951

  The rapidity of a biased coin is its distance from fairness
  in information geometry. Maximum rapidity = certainty (p=0 or p=1).

  In tournaments: each arc T[i][j] is a biased coin (0 or 1).
  The average rapidity of a tournament's arcs measures its
  DISTANCE FROM THE RANDOM TOURNAMENT in information space.

============================================================
7. THE RAPIDITY OF THE TRANSFER MATRIX EIGENVALUES
============================================================

  Transfer matrix M(x) char poly: lambda^3 - lambda^2 - x*lambda - x = 0
  At x = tanh(phi), the eigenvalues live in rapidity space.

  The EP eigenvalue d = 1/phi has Q(d) = Q(1/phi) = phi^3.
  EP rapidity = arctanh(1/phi) = 0.7218177376
  = (3/2)*ln(phi) = 0.7218177376

  The tribonacci eigenvalue at x=1: lambda = tau.
  But tau > 1, so arctanh(tau) is complex!
  arctanh(tau) = arctanh(1.839287)
  = (1/2)*ln((1+tau)/(tau-1))
  = (1/2)*ln(3.382976)
  = 0.609378
  + i*pi/2  (because tau > 1, we're past the pole)

  The tribonacci lives PAST the rapidity singularity at v=1 (speed of light).
  Its rapidity has an imaginary part = pi/2: it's a TACHYON!

  In our theory: x=1 is the pole of Q. For x < 1 (subluminal),
  rapidity is real. For x > 1 (superluminal), rapidity gains i*pi/2.
  The tribonacci constant tau ~ 1.839 is SUPERLUMINAL.
  Its rapidity = ln(tau^2)/2 + i*pi/2 = ln(tau) + i*pi/2.

