  The forbidden rapidities:
  rapidity(7)  = ln(7)/2  = 0.972955
  rapidity(21) = ln(21)/2 = 1.522261
  rapidity(21) - rapidity(7) = ln(3)/2 = 0.549306 = rapidity(3)

  The GAP between the two forbidden rapidities is EXACTLY
  the rapidity of 3 = the curvature quantum = one OCTAVE!
  H=7 and H=21 are separated by exactly one octave in rapidity space.

============================================================
9. THE HARMONIC SERIES IN RAPIDITY SPACE
============================================================

  arctanh(x) = x + x^3/3 + x^5/5 + x^7/7 + ...
  Each term x^k/k contributes rapidity x^k/k to the total.

  At x = 1/(2n+1) (the musical inputs):
  arctanh(1/(2n+1)) = sum_{j=0}^inf 1/((2j+1)*(2n+1)^{2j+1})
  The leading term 1/(2n+1) dominates. Higher terms decay as 1/(2n+1)^3.

  But for the FULL arctanh, the terms form a series of rapidities:
  x + x^3/3 + x^5/5 + ...
  = rapidity(fundamental) + rapidity(3rd harmonic)/3 + rapidity(5th)/5 + ...

  This is a FOURIER-LIKE decomposition of rapidity into harmonics!
  arctanh = sum of ODD HARMONICS of the rapidity.

  In music: the odd harmonics 1, 3, 5, 7, ... are the overtone series
  of a CLOSED PIPE (clarinet, organ stopped pipe).
  Open pipes have ALL harmonics. Closed pipes have only ODD ones.

  arctanh IS the closed-pipe harmonic series.
  artanh(x) = clarinet playing note x.
  tanh(x) = the inverse: which note produces this timbre?

