  = (10/21)/(22/21) = 10/22 = 5/11 EXACTLY!
  1/5 (+) 1/7 = 0.3333333333
  = (12/35)/(36/35) = 12/36 = 1/3 EXACTLY!

  1/5 (+) 1/7 = 1/3!
  THE FIFTH COMPOSED WITH THE FOURTH GIVES THE OCTAVE.
  This is the musical identity: fifth + fourth = octave.
  But now it's a RELATIVISTIC velocity addition identity!

  1/3 (+) 1/7 = 5/11.
  The octave composed with the fourth gives 5/11.
  5 and 11 are PALEY PRIMES.

  GENERAL FORMULA:
  1/(2a+1) (+) 1/(2b+1) = (2a+2b+2) / (2(2ab+a+b+1))
  = (a+b+1) / (2ab+a+b+1)

    1/3 (+) 1/5 = 1/2 = 0.500000   (verify: True)
    1/3 (+) 1/7 = 5/11 = 0.454545   (verify: True)
    1/5 (+) 1/7 = 1/3 = 0.333333   (verify: True)
    1/3 (+) 1/9 = 3/7 = 0.428571   (verify: True)
    1/5 (+) 1/9 = 7/23 = 0.304348   (verify: True)
    1/7 (+) 1/9 = 1/4 = 0.250000   (verify: True)

  When does 1/(2a+1) (+) 1/(2b+1) = 1/(2c+1) for integer c?
  Need: (a+b+1)/(2ab+a+b+1) = 1/(2c+1)
  => 2c+1 = (2ab+a+b+1)/(a+b+1)
  => (2ab+a+b+1) = (2c+1)(a+b+1)
  => 2ab+a+b+1 = 2ac+2bc+a+b+2c+1
  => 2ab = 2c(a+b+1)
  => c = ab/(a+b+1)

  c must be a positive integer. So (a+b+1) | ab.
  Check: a=2, b=3: c = 6/6 = 1. YES! 1/5 (+) 1/7 = 1/3.
  Check: a=1, b=2: c = 2/4 = 1/2. NO (not integer).
  Check: a=1, b=3: c = 3/5. NO.
  Check: a=3, b=5: c = 15/9 = 5/3. NO.
  Check: a=5, b=9: c = 45/15 = 3. YES! 1/11 (+) 1/19 = 1/7.

  1/11 (+) 1/19 = 1/7!
  The MINOR THIRD composed with the UNDECIMAL gives the FOURTH.
  And 11, 19 are Paley primes; 7 is the threshold.

  Verify: 1/11 (+) 1/19 = 0.1428571429 = 1/7 = 0.1428571429
  Match: True

